    "result": "I implemented `search_products` in `solution.py`, and all 13 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass. I didn't run a coverage report, so the 90% gate is unchecked. The tests exercise every branch of the function, so I expect it to clear.\n\n- **Filtering:** it keeps only products with `stock > 0`, matches `name_contains` as an ASCII case-insensitive substring using `LIKE ... ESCAPE`, so `%` and `_` are literal, and applies `max_price` when given.\n- **Ordering and paging:** it sorts by `name` or `price`, descending if asked, with ties always broken by ascending `id`. `limit` and `offset` apply after that.\n- **Validation:** it raises `ValueError` for a bad `order_by`, a `limit` outside 1–100, or an `offset` below 0. It also rejects non-integer values and booleans for `limit` and `offset`, which the spec doesn't state. It only reads from the database.\n\nTwo of my first test expectations were wrong about binary name ordering, not the code. I corrected them, and the tests now show that uppercase sorts before lowercase and that a space sorts before `%`.",
